  "notes": "{送金|そうきん} means sending money to another person or institution. Compound of ⟦{送|おく}る→送る：00742_okuru⟧ (send) + {金|きん} (money). Used as a ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ verb: {送金|そうきん}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {送金|そうきん}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to send money, to remit\n- {送金|そうきん}⟦{手数料|てすうりょう}→手数料：05423_tesuuryou⟧: remittance/transfer fee\n- {海外|かいがい}{送金|そうきん}: overseas remittance\n- ⟦{銀行|ぎんこう}→銀行：00578_ginkou⟧{送金|そうきん}: bank transfer\n- {送金|そうきん}{先|さき}: remittance destination\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {送金|そうきん}: general term for sending money (any method)\n- {振|ふ}り{込|こ}み: bank transfer (specifically into a bank account)\n- ⟦{振|ふ}り{込|こ}む→振り込む：10992_furikomu⟧: to make a bank transfer (verb)\n- ⟦{為替|かわせ}→為替：04021_kawase⟧: money order or foreign exchange\n\nREGISTER:\nSomewhat formal. In everyday speech, ⟦{振|ふ}り{込|こ}む→振り込む：10992_furikomu⟧ is more commonly used for domestic bank transfers.",
